Description: GHSA-fpwc-w8rq-cr92: on a redirect to another origin (scheme, host or port) the http:// stream wrapper drops Authorization, Cookie and Proxy-Authorization from the header option of the context, repeated headers, folded values and whitespace before the colon included; with it GH-11274: 307 and 308 redirects keep the method (POST, PATCH) and the body, as RFC 7231 and RFC 7538 require. The fixes of 7.4 for an empty and a 1-character Location (GH-23467, GH-23521) do not apply: 5.6 does not follow an empty Location and reads it from a fixed-size buffer.
Origin: php-src commits c812ca1d4d42 (GH-11274, Niels Dossche) and dc1f36a75a77 (14.09.2026, Alexandre Daubois, Jakub Zelenka) of the PHP 7.4 security branch of Remi Collet (remicollet/php-src-security PHP-7.4-security-backports)

